<section class="section"><div class="wrap article-layout"><article class="article-body">
<h2>Professional focus</h2><p>Ozan Ferhat Şen began his legal education at Dicle University Faculty of Law in 2010. As real estate and construction matters became an increasingly significant part of his professional practice, he continued his academic development in the Real Estate and Construction Law graduate program at Istanbul University Institute of Social Sciences.</p><p>His legal work focuses particularly on real estate, construction, zoning and the legal issues that arise around property development and urban transformation.</p>
<h2>Property problems rarely stay in one legal box</h2><p>A title-deed issue may lead to a zoning question. A zoning problem may affect a construction project. A construction agreement may become central to an urban transformation process. This overlap is one reason the English section of this website is organised around the underlying legal problem rather than around the client’s nationality.</p><p>International property owners, buyers and investors can therefore access the same core practice areas in English: <a href="/en/real-estate-law-turkey/">real estate law</a>, <a href="/en/zoning-planning-law-turkey/">zoning and planning law</a>, <a href="/en/construction-law-turkey/">construction law</a> and <a href="/en/urban-transformation-law-turkey/">urban transformation law</a>.</p>
<h2>English-language coordination</h2><p>International clients may need legal documents, transaction steps and Turkish administrative terminology explained clearly in English. English-language enquiries and practical coordination are available through the dedicated international contact number shown on the English pages. Legal advice, legal assessment and legal strategy are provided by Attorney Ozan Ferhat Şen.</p>
<h2>Beyond law</h2><p>Outside legal practice, his two principal interests are music and mathematics. His interest in mathematics also extends to teaching and educational content production.</p>
